        q: "Why does a parameterised query prevent SQL injection?",
        options: ["It removes all quotes from input", "It encrypts the query", "It limits input length", "The SQL structure is parsed first and values are always treated as data"],
        answer: 3,
        why: "Values never pass through the SQL parser as code, so they cannot change the query.",
